## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design a production-ready online continual learning system under delayed feedback, latency, memory limits, and non-stationary user behavior, with fairness concerns.

## Key Concepts

- Online continual learning with delayed labels
- Factorization machines and warm-start online SGD
- Calibration, drift detection, and memory-budget governance

## Code Example

```javascript
// Skeleton online update loop for streaming features
function onlineUpdate(x, y, w, lr) {
  const pred = 1 / (1 + Math.exp(-dot(w, x)));
  const g = pred - y;
  for (let i = 0; i < x.length; i++) w[i] -= lr * g * x[i];
  return w;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you monitor for calibration drift in production?
- How would you enforce fairness constraints without sacrificing overall performance?

## Why This Question Is Asked
Evaluates the ability to design real-world, latency-constrained explainability systems that balance privacy and governance requirements in high-stakes ML environments.

## Key Concepts
- Per-instance explanations under strict latency constraints
- Privacy-preserving attribution without raw feature exposure
- Caching, bucketing, and surrogate models for performance optimization
- Drift monitoring and governance compliance

## Code Example
```javascript
function attribution(event) {
  const bucket = features.map(f => bucketize(f.value, f.schema));
  const fingerprint = hash(bucket);
  const cached = cache.get(fingerprint);
  if (cached) return cached;
  const attribution = surrogate.predict(bucket);
  cache.set(fingerprint, attribution);
  return attribution;
}
```

